  <symbol id="i-source" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
    <path d="m8.5 8.5-4.5 3.5 4.5 3.5"/>
    <path d="m15.5 8.5 4.5 3.5-4.5 3.5"/>
    <path d="m13.5 5.5-3 13"/>
  </symbol>

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
     Imported icons — everything in src/assets/icons/

     Each .svg in that folder is inlined below at build time as
     <symbol id="i-<filename>">. So linkedin-with-circle.svg becomes
     <use href="#i-linkedin-with-circle">. Drop a file in and it works; to
     update an icon, replace the file. No path data is copied by hand.

     A path's `d` attribute takes drawing commands, not a filename — which
     is why referencing the file there could never work. This reads the
     file and pulls its real geometry in.

     The importer also strips <title>/<desc> so they do not surface as
     tooltips, namespaces internal ids so two icons cannot collide over
     id="a", and rewrites hardcoded black fills to currentColor so an icon
     takes the colour of the link containing it.

     Tip: name files after the id you want. github.svg is nicer to reference
     than github-with-circle-and-shadow.svg.

     Brand marks: using the GitHub or LinkedIn logo to link to your own
     profile is ordinary nominative use. Keep the shape unmodified and leave
     clear space around it.
     --------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  {% iconSprite %}

